        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260513-trump-set-to-meet-with-xi-in-beijing-as-war-and-inflation-weigh-on-his-presidency",
        "orario": "11:43",
        "timestamp": 1778665415,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump set to meet with Xi in Beijing as war and inflation weigh on his presidency Issued on: 13/05/2026 - 11:43 US President Donald Trump is set to arrive in Beijing on Wednesday for his highly anticipated summit with Chinese leader Xi Jinping at a restless moment for a world worried about war, trade and artificial intelligence. While Trump likes to project a sense of strength, the visit occurs at a delicate moment for his presidency as his popularity at home has been weighed down by the US and Israel's war with Iran and rising inflation as a consequence of that conflict. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert tells us more. France intensifies hantavirus surveillance as 22 contact cases identified 13/05/2026 Hantavirus: How was ‘patient zero’ infected? 13/05/2026 Macron's interview with FRANCE 24: French president recaps his work in Africa over 2 terms 13/05/2026 Who walks the red carpet at Cannes? 13/05/2026 How Keir Starmer could be replaced as UK PM after discontent rises in his own party 13/05/2026 79th Cannes Film Festival: Inside the making of the prestigious Palme d’Or 13/05/2026 WHO praises Spain's handling of repatriation: 'Further Hantavirus spread can be stopped effectively' 13/05/2026 Health Hantavirus vs. Covid: Low transmission efficiency means far less risk of another widespread outbreak 13/05/2026 Health 'Serious disease': Hantavirus less infectious than COVID, yet has significant fatality rate - 1 in 3 13/05/2026 Health"
