        "timestamp": 1778665337,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. France intensifies hantavirus surveillance as 22 contact cases identified Issued on: 13/05/2026 - 11:42 The hantavirus outbreak has now reached 11 total reported cases, 9 of which have been confirmed. In France, a woman infected in the deadly virus outbreak on a cruise ship is critically ill, a doctor at the Paris hospital caring for the sickened passenger said Tuesday. With 22 contact cases in the country overall, authorities say there is no widespread transmission of the virus at this moment. Hantavirus: How was ‘patient zero’ infected? 13/05/2026 Macron's interview with FRANCE 24: French president recaps his work in Africa over 2 terms 13/05/2026 Who walks the red carpet at Cannes? 13/05/2026 How Keir Starmer could be replaced as UK PM after discontent rises in his own party 13/05/2026 79th Cannes Film Festival: Inside the making of the prestigious Palme d’Or 13/05/2026 WHO praises Spain's handling of repatriation: 'Further Hantavirus spread can be stopped effectively' 13/05/2026 Health Hantavirus vs. Covid: Low transmission efficiency means far less risk of another widespread outbreak 13/05/2026 Health 'Serious disease': Hantavirus less infectious than COVID, yet has significant fatality rate - 1 in 3 13/05/2026 Health Trump 'could choose to change Taiwan policy in Beijing' unhindered by Congress, analyst says 12/05/2026 Asia / Pacific"
